Usage:
  gbridge hook install             start a background sync on every git push from this machine (Git 2.54+)
  gbridge hook install --per-repo  for older Git: write a pre-push hook into each source repo's .git/hooks
  gbridge hook uninstall           remove the push hook from global git config and every source repo
  gbridge hook status              show the push hook, the source repos it covers, and the last background sync

No repo's tracked files change. Leave one repo out: git config hook.gbridge.enabled false
Background sync output goes to sync.log in the greenbridge home.
